OK, so the nozzle tilting code at line 467-470 is:
```typescript
if (!isCenter) {
    const dir = new THREE.Vector3(0, tipY, 0).sub(pos).normalize();
    group.quaternion.setFromUnitVectors(new THREE.Vector3(0, -1, 0), dir);
}
```

This makes every non-center nozzle point toward the center-bottom point `(0, tipY, 0)`. This is the intentional design - outer nozzles tilt inward to converge toward a point.


The user is saying this tilting behavior wasn't there originally, so I need to compare the current commit against the previous one to see when this nozzle rotation logic was introduced.

